{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 21, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "Arthur blinked, the harsh sunlight surprisingly vivid. He sat up in bed, the floral pattern of the comforter feeling oddly…pixelated. A notification box, shimmering with a faint blue outline, floated in his vision: \"Welcome to Aethelgard! Level 1 Awakened. Quest: Find the Lost Amulet of Eldoria.\" He scrambled out of bed, his hand passing right through the wooden nightstand. Panic flared. He looked at his reflection in the antique mirror - sharper features, slightly exaggerated musculature, and a ridiculously heroic jawline. A system menu popped up: \"Stats: Strength 10, Dexterity 8, Intelligence 6. Health: 100/100.\" This wasn't his bedroom. This wasn't his life. He was *in* a video game.\n\n***\n\nHe cautiously ventured outside, the cobblestone streets of a medieval village feeling unnervingly real. Villagers with overly expressive faces stared, their dialogue options appearing as text bubbles above their heads. A gruff-looking blacksmith offered him a quest: \"Fetch me 10 iron ore. Reward: Rusty Sword.\" Arthur sighed, a hollow sound in the crisp morning air. He had no idea how to play this game, what the rules were, or how to get back to his own reality. But one thing was clear: he was no longer Arthur Penhaligon, accountant. He was now…something else. And he had an amulet to find.\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "Arthur", "logprob": -0.16696929931640625}, {"token": "▁blinked", "logprob": -0.407365083694458}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.00015984688070602715}, {"token": "▁the", "logprob": -0.08786557614803314}, {"token": "▁harsh", "logprob": -1.1052302122116089}, {"token": "▁sunlight", "logprob": -0.006520306225866079}, {"token": "▁surprisingly", "logprob": -1.248792290687561}, {"token": "▁vivid", "logprob": -2.149542808532715}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.015251445583999157}, {"token": "▁He", "logprob": -0.010840335860848427}, {"token": "▁sat", "logprob